                        "entry_id": "34b8c61f-b6fc-3087-8dfa-fcec03f0dcbf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A seasoned, battered and fried potato wedge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British-Columbia",
                            "Northwestern",
                            "US",
                            "in-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11706b95-7f9e-4d00-8b76-fae7bcac31a3",
                                "sense_id": "66873f01-2f6d-31d6-a6ee-bc6497529a28",
                                "text": "If you're really hungry, be sure to try the wood-fired jojos (potato wedges)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b77443e-691f-4137-8f28-6ebfd7e7be8e",
                                "sense_id": "66873f01-2f6d-31d6-a6ee-bc6497529a28",
                                "text": "The cheesy jojos threaten to colonize every inch of my appetite but I hold back by only eating them once I am nearly full."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76f85a65-4dee-4854-844a-adaf0ae5aba1",
                                "sense_id": "66873f01-2f6d-31d6-a6ee-bc6497529a28",
                                "text": "And perhaps George's best (un)kept secret is its fried chicken and jojos, which give Reel M Inn a run for its money."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
